[clarity]  10.5 min  WREN: Wait. Hold it up to the light.
[clarity]  10.6 min  beam: site 0 (31, 1)
[clarity]  10.6 min  WREN: That's a Settler seed tin. Cradle stamp on the lid. One of ours, left behind in the rush.
[clarity]  10.6 min  card: Plant the first seed | Plants fill your Bloom Core.
[clarity]  10.7 min  WREN: When they left, the Settlers sealed every seed they could carry into the Cradle's vault. Your vault, Lumi.
[orbit-perf] process_ms avg=35.77 max=45.87 physics_ms avg=53.37 junk=10536 (near 1648 far 9058) junk_ms=0 mounds=0 landmarks=0 draw_calls=0 prims=0 streamer={"apply_us_max":5316,"apply_us_sum":46628,"build_us_max":432241,"build_us_sum":3204363,"built":37,"chunk_tris":79546,"collide":2,"horizon_m":434.745341318179,"jobs":2,"lod0":7,"lod1":12,"lod2":0,"near":69,"pending":2,"shell_ms":192,"shell_tris":61440,"view_alt":2.27907905229222}
[clarity]  10.8 min  card: Plant the first seed
[clarity]  10.8 min  WREN: The plan was simple. Wait for the dust to settle. Come home. Plant. They called that day the Greenfall.
[clarity]  10.9 min  WREN: Then three hundred years went by, and the dust never settled. Until a seed-keeper fell out of the sky.
[clarity]  11.0 min  WREN: Nothing grows on its own anymore. The soil forgot how. Somebody has to put it in the ground.
[clarity]  11.1 min  WREN: That somebody is you. Small. Stubborn. Running on four percent. Perfect.
